<section class="case-sec" id="rubric">
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="sec-mark">§D — Trust is a number: the confidence rubric</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        The agent is not allowed to sound more certain than its evidence. Every
        finding is scored against a fixed rubric before it reaches the bridge —
        and the score changes what the agent may say.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
    <div class="cp-head"><span>// confidence rubric — enforced on every finding</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Score</th><th>Evidence bar</th><th>What the agent may claim</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td class="num good">HIGH</td>
            <td>≥2 independent tools agree · timelines align · row-count assertions passed</td>
            <td>A probable cause, stated as such, with a recommended mitigation path</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="num">MED</td>
            <td>Single-source evidence, or agreeing sources with a timeline gap</td>
            <td>A hypothesis worth a human's next 10 minutes — never a conclusion</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td class="num warn">LOW</td>
            <td>Inference without direct data, or tools returned zero rows</td>
            <td>"Insufficient evidence" — plus exactly which query would resolve it</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="board-foot">// a zero-row query is reported as <span class="g">no data</span>, never as "no issues found."</div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-sec" id="evals">
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="sec-mark">§E — Evals decide whether to trust it</div>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        An agent that briefs incident bridges doesn't get to be evaluated on
        vibes. The harness replays a golden set of <strong>historical incidents with
        known root causes</strong> — investigations where the ground truth was
        established the hard way — and scores every prompt, tool, and model
        change before it ships, exactly like CI.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="table-panel panel reveal">
    <div class="cp-head"><span>// eval dimensions — replayed-incident golden set</span><span class="g">gates every change</span></div>
    <div class="table-scroll">
      <table class="data-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>Question it answers</th><th>Failure it exists to catch</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td class="mono">root-cause hit</td><td>Did the top-ranked hypothesis match the incident's established cause?</td><td>Confident, coherent, wrong</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">citation validity</td><td>Does every numeric claim resolve to a real query ID with matching rows?</td><td>Narratives that outrun their evidence</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">hypothesis discipline</td><td>Were wrong theories killed by a tool result, not silently dropped?</td><td>Anchoring on the first plausible story</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">tool budget</td><td>Did the run stay inside its call and token budgets?</td><td>Runaway loops that cost more than the incident</td></tr>
          <tr><td class="mono">calibration</td><td>Do HIGH-confidence verdicts match ground truth more often than MED?</td><td>A rubric that's theater instead of a control</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    <div class="board-foot">// per-dimension scores are internal and stay internal — <span class="g">the gate, not the grade, is the point.</span></div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="case-sec" id="changed">
  <div class="reveal">
    <div class="sec-mark">§F — What it changed</div>
  </div>
  <div class="metric-row panel reveal">
    <div class="m"><span class="v">hrs → min</span><span class="d">Sev2 investigation time, end to end</span></div>
    <div class="m"><span class="v">10</span><span class="d">MCP tools dispatched concurrently against live systems</span></div>
    <div class="m"><span class="v">2</span><span class="d">reusable MCP servers now serving other agents &amp; Copilot</span></div>
    <div class="m"><span class="v">100%</span><span class="d">of runs traced — every claim resolves to a query ID</span></div>
  </div>
  <div class="prose reveal">
    <p>
      The quieter outcome is who acts on it: the agent's brief is the first
      artifact on the bridge, and the on-call validates instead of hunts. During
      a <strong>4-team cross-org Sev2</strong> that same discipline — hypotheses, evidence,
      cited claims — is what let one person run the room.
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

